    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Jackson Merrill**, who sits at the top of our board with a 75.10 efficiency score. Facing Trey Yesavage (4.55 xERA), **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a potent combination of a favorable SP matchup and a significant boost from his projected #2 spot in the lineup. Close behind, **Kyle Tucker** (69.61) and **Gunnar Henderson** (71.11) serve as our core anchors. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a slightly tougher path against Cameron, his elite plate appearance profile and leadoff role remain too valuable to fade. **Coby Mayo** (66.04) also warrants attention; despite the risk of an elite hold pitcher, the park factors in his favor provide the necessary leverage to keep him firmly in the 1B slot.\n\nOur decision-making process was most tested at the utility and bench spots. **Miguel Vargas** (51.83) was the strongest contender from the bench, but he fell just short of displacing our starters due to the high efficiency scores of **Andy Pages** (66.83) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.76). **Andy Pages** is a particularly interesting play today; his efficiency is bolstered by a +2% bump due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an prime environment for stealing bases\u2014a priority for the Waves given our scarcity strategy. Meanwhile, we are closely monitoring the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, all of whom are currently \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have modeled their production based on historical slotting, any late-breaking lineup changes could force a rotation toward bench assets like **Brayan Rocchio** or **Curtis Mead**. \n\nFinally, please note that while **Jorge Polanco** (44.24) remains on the bench for purely efficiency-based reasons, he carries a 45% rain risk warning, further justifying his omission. We are otherwise positioned to exploit the weak xERA marks of the opposing staff, particularly the middle-of-the-road matchups for **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, and **Heliot Ramos**, all of whom are safely in the \"Strong\" category to help us maintain our competitive standing in 5x5 Roto.",
